    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've got a heifer that just came out of rumenotomy about 6 hours ago. I need a clear protocol for what I should be looking out for over the next few days regarding the incision site and any internal signs of trouble or infection. Also, what's the plan for getting her back on feed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Post-surgery, the incision site should be monitored daily for signs of infection, like redness, swelling, discharge, or heat around the incision. Watch for any discomfort or behavioral changes indicating pain. As for her internal condition, check for normal rumination, alertness, dental alignment, hoof health, and appetite. If she's not experiencing discomfort, resume feeding with a small amount of hay at first, progressively increasing as tolerated. For six weeks, keep her on a well-balanced diet, gradually introducing grain as her rumen readjusts. Check with a veterinarian if you notice any concerning symptoms.",
      "source": "target",
